{
  "note": "Re-judged 2026-09-30 after D-8. The recorded weak verdict named the missing clause: an Accept authorizing an unavailable service through an attribute other than Service-Type, for example Framed-User over Framed-Protocol SLIP on the L2TP LNS. That clause is now asserted: TestRFC2865AcceptForAFramingTheLNSLacksIsRejected sends Framed-User with Framed-Protocol 2, 3, 4, 5, 6 (every RFC 2865 Section 5.7 framing but PPP) and 255, and fails if the session comes up; TestRFC2865AcceptForPPPFramingIsHonored sends Framed-User over PPP and fails if it is refused. Service-Type is Framed-User in both, so only the framing varies. Producer: doRADIUS refuses unless radius.AcceptedFramedProtocol(resp, FramedProtocolPPP); an absent Framed-Protocol is accepted (TestRFC2865SupportedServiceTypeIsHonored carries none and is honored, so no regression). The author observed the negative red at Framed-Protocol 2 before the fix; the gate records are panic breaks on AcceptedFramedProtocol (positive) and doRADIUS (negative). The Service-Type units on the admin and L2TP paths are unchanged and still cover the Service-Type route. Service and framing are the two attributes RFC 2865 uses to authorize a service (Section 1.1 names ARAP, a framing, as its example), so both routes are now enforced.",
